   ],
   "authority_doc": "docs/ui/LENSES.md",
   "design": "Ruled 2026-08-25 (Ben, looking at the live Throughput lens): \"when a lens needs a legend, it takes the minimap space\" — the flush-left-of-the-minimap anchor is retired, because it put the key over the always-open Selection band and read as sloppy. Design settled in docs/ui/LENSES.md § legend chromes; read it before implementing. Scope: move the gradient-bar chrome (begin_lens_key) into the minimap rect and let the minimap yield; the count-driven keys already sit in the right chrome column above the minimap and should be reconciled to the same rule rather than left as a second idiom. Two consequences fall out and are deliberately part of this item: the BL-376 foreground-list + opaque-fill workaround becomes unnecessary once the legend owns its rect (it was the right fix for the wrong layout), which also dissolves the standing defect that six of the seven gradient keys were unreadable under the band; and the item must answer what the minimap does while displaced — hidden outright, or restored the moment the lens clears. A live click is required, per the UI rule. CANCELLED 2026-08-25, by Ben on seeing the merged build: \"Looks fantastic, probably better than my direct instruction to fill minimap space.\" Sprint 17b had already moved every legend into one chrome home — the minimap HEADER, growing upward into the column — which answers the complaint that prompted the ruling (a key popped out over the Selection band) without taking the minimap's own rect. The 2026-08-25 ruling is therefore superseded by its own author in favour of what shipped. The z-order half of this item is also moot: 17b's region overlaps no window, so the foreground-list workaround was dropped at the merge rather than generalised. RENUMBERED BL-604 -> BL-609 on 2026-08-25. Sprint 17b and Sprint 18 ran concurrently on 2026-08-24 and both drew BL-604 from the same fresh id range for different work; 17b's landed in a FROZEN cold archive and holds the majority of live citations, so Sprint 18's id moved instead. Commit messages written before this pass still cite the old id — they are immutable and the mapping is recorded here."
  },
